    description: 'Americana tradition (1990-present), emerging from Uncle Tupelo (1987-1994) and No Depression magazine community. Ensemble: acoustic-and-electric guitar, pedal steel or lap steel, fiddle or mandolin, upright or electric bass, drum kit with country-rock backbeat. Repertoire mixes country, folk-revival, garage-rock, and singer-songwriter idioms. Distinguished from mainstream-country by deliberate-roughness and rejection of Nashville production; distinguished from country-rock by 1990s-onward timeline and indie-label distribution. Wilco, Drive-By Truckers, Lucinda Williams, Whiskeytown codified the regional sound; Americana Music Association founded 2000.',
