    description: 'Southern-Italian processional and pastorale tradition: tarantella (Apulia and Calabria), pizzica-pizzica (Salento), tammurriata (Campania), saltarello (Lazio). Zampogna-ciaramella pastoral pipe-couple tradition associated with Christmas novena processions through Naples and Rome (18th-century-onward). Tambourine-driven dance-trance practice (pizzica especially) historically connected to tarantismo healing-ritual. Distinguished from Sardinian tradition by mainland-Italian language and by Catholic-ritual-calendar context. Revival movement since 1970s through Notte della Taranta festival and ethnomusicological collecting.',
