    axes: { harm: -1, pitch: 0, ornament: 2, meter: 0, density: -1, transmission: 2, improv: 1, soundTech: -2, intensity: 1, voice: 2, timbre: 1, percussion: 0, cyclicity: 0 },
    description: 'Armenian liturgical-and-folk tradition associated with Komitas Vardapet (1869-1935), who collected and transcribed pre-Soviet Armenian peasant-and-liturgical melody. Armenian Apostolic liturgy uses sharakan (hymns) in 8-mode (oktoechos) system. Folk repertoire includes ashugh (bardic-poet) song, dance-tune, and lyric-song. Iconic instruments: duduk (apricot-wood double-reed, deep-mournful timbre), kanun (plucked zither shared with Anatolian-Arab tradition), oud, dhol drum. Distinguished from neighboring Turkish-makam by Armenian-modal organization and by specifically-Armenian liturgical context.',
    exemplars: ['Djivan Gasparyan — duduk solo recordings', 'Komitas Quartet — Komitas-transcription recordings', 'Lusine Zakharyan — sharakan-cycle albums', 'Hasmik Harutyunyan — folk-song recordings'],
