    axes: { harm: 0, pitch: 1, ornament: 2, meter: 1, density: 1, transmission: 1, improv: 2, soundTech: -1, intensity: 1, voice: 1, timbre: 1, percussion: 1, cyclicity: 0 },
    description: 'Turkish-Romani çümbüş music: urban-Anatolian Roma musical practice including 9/8 karşılama (greeting-dance), wedding-music ensemble work, and meyhane (tavern) performance. Çümbüş (metal-resonator-bodied fretless lute, invented 1930 by Zeynel Abidin Cümbüş) is regional-iconic. Standard ensemble adds kanun, clarinet (uniquely-prominent in Turkish-Romani context, often G-clarinet), darbuka. Distinguished from Anatolian-rural folk by urban-context and Roma-community origin; distinguished from Greek-rebetiko by Turkish-makam-not-Greek-makam organization.',
