    description: 'Japanese-language hip-hop tradition emerging in 1980s and 1990s through Vibrastone, ECD, and the broader Tokyo-based underground scene. The 2000s commercial peak through KICK THE CAN CREW, KREVA, and the Mary Joy Recordings roster brought J-rap into mainstream-J-pop visibility. The 2010s-2020s wave through KOHH, Awich, JP THE WAVY, and the Bad Hop crew consolidated the contemporary scene. Distinguished by Japanese-language wordplay-density and explicit Japanese-cultural lyrical content.',
    exemplars: ['ECD', 'KREVA', 'KICK THE CAN CREW', 'KOHH', 'Awich', 'JP THE WAVY'],
