    axes: { harm: 2, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 2, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 1, voice: 2, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 1 },
    description: 'Early-2000s UK electronic-and-jazz fusion subgenre extending broken beat into deeper jazz-and-soul integration. 4hero\'s Two Pages (1998) and Creating Patterns (2001), and Bugz in the Attic\'s 2000-2005 work, defined the canonical aesthetic. Distinguished from drum-and-bass by broken beat\'s slower-tempo (108-115 BPM) and explicit jazz-fusion harmonic-vocabulary.',
    exemplars: ['4hero', 'IG Culture', 'Bugz in the Attic', 'Domu', 'Kaidi Tatham', 'Bahia Black'],
