    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 0, meter: 2, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 1, voice: 1, timbre: 1, percussion: 2, cyclicity: 1 },
    description: 'Mid-2010s Australian electronic subgenre developed by Flume (Harley Streten, Sydney) characterized by chopped-pitched-vocal sampling, metallic-wobble synth-bass leads, half-time drum-machine programming, and emotional-melodic content. Flume\'s self-titled debut (2012) and Skin (2016) inaugurated the canonical sound; Cashmere Cat, San Holo, Marshmello, and the broader Mad Decent and OWSLA label rosters extended the genre.',
    exemplars: ['Flume', 'Cashmere Cat', 'San Holo', 'Marshmello', 'Louis the Child', 'Future Classic Records'],
