    axes: { harm: 1, pitch: 1, ornament: 1, meter: 1, density: 2, transmission: 1, improv: 1, soundTech: 1, intensity: 0, voice: -2, timbre: 2, percussion: 0, cyclicity: 0 },
    description: 'Late-1990s and 2000s electronic subgenre developed primarily in Germany (Oval, Mille Plateaux label) and Austria (Fennesz), characterized by deliberate use of digital-error sounds (CD-skips, microsound cuts, glitches) as primary compositional material. Oval\'s 94diskont (1995), Fennesz\'s Endless Summer (2001), and the broader Mille Plateaux Records and Touch Records rosters anchor the canonical glitch aesthetic.',
