    description: '2010s alternative R&B subgenre emphasizing emotional-vulnerability, experimental-electronic production, atmospheric-vocal layering, and explicit indie-rock-aesthetic-influence over the broader commercial R&B mainstream. FKA twigs\' EP1 (2012) and LP1 (2014) inaugurated the canonical British alt-R&B sound; Jhené Aiko, Banks, Kelela, Tinashe (early career), and the broader Top Dawg Entertainment and Atlantic Records alt-R&B rosters extended the genre.',
