    description: 'Mid-1990s indie rock subgenre characterized by complex polymetric rhythmic structures (irregular time signatures, frequent meter changes), angular and arpeggiated guitar-line architecture, and explicit prog-rock-influenced compositional ambition. Slint\'s Spiderland (1991) inaugurated the canonical sound; Don Caballero (Pittsburgh), Shellac (Steve Albini), Polvo, and the broader Touch and Go-Quarterstick label rosters defined the canonical American math rock roster. The Japanese math-rock scene (Toe, Tricot) extended international influence.',
    exemplars: ['Slint', 'Don Caballero', 'Shellac', 'Polvo', 'Toe (Japanese)', 'Tricot (Japanese)'],
