    description: 'Late-1980s and 1990s American post-hardcore subgenre developed from 1980s hardcore-punk through more melodic and experimental compositional approach. Fugazi (Washington D.C., 1987-2003), Drive Like Jehu, Quicksand, Refused, At the Drive-In, and the broader Dischord Records label roster anchor the canonical American post-hardcore roster. Direct ancestor of 2000s screamo, midwest emo, and broader emocore developments.',
