    description: '2000s and 2010s Korean independent music scene developing alongside the broader K-pop industry but with distinctly indie-rock and folk-rock aesthetic. Hongdae neighborhood of Seoul anchors institutional infrastructure (the area\'s many small-venues, including FF Club, V-Hall, and Club Spot). Hyukoh, Jaurim, Jannabi, Crying Nut (foundational 1990s), and the broader Magic Strawberry Sound and Pastel Music label rosters anchor the canonical K-indie roster.',
