    description: 'Modern Mandarin Chinese popular music developed from 2000s onward through Jay Chou\'s post-2000 commercial peak and the broader Taiwanese and Mainland Chinese market. Characterized by sophisticated R&B-and-hip-hop-influenced production, romantic-ballad emphasis, and contemporary Mandarin-pop commercial-radio aesthetic. Jay Chou, JJ Lin, Eason Chan (Cantopop crossover), G.E.M., and the contemporary Mainland Chinese reality-show winners constitute the canonical contemporary mandopop roster.',
