    description: 'Early-1990s UK electronic subgenre developed in 1990-1993 London through synthesis of Belgian new-beat, Detroit techno, and US house with chopped-Amen-break percussion, ragga-MC vocal-sampling, and rapidly-accelerating tempo (138-150 BPM and rising toward jungle\'s 170+). The 1991 Acen "Trip to the Moon", 1992 SL2 "On a Ragga Tip", and the broader Production House and Suburban Base label rosters consolidated the canonical sound. Direct ancestor of jungle and drum-and-bass.',
