    description: '1970s jazz subgenre developed from Miles Davis\'s late-1960s Bitches Brew sessions, integrating jazz-improvisational practice with rock-and-funk rhythmic vocabulary and electric-amplified-instrumentation. Weather Report (founded 1970 by Joe Zawinul and Wayne Shorter), Mahavishnu Orchestra (John McLaughlin), Return to Forever (Chick Corea), and Headhunters (Herbie Hancock) constitute the canonical 1970s fusion roster. Distinguished from broader jazz by fusion\'s explicit rock-and-funk-rhythmic-electric-instrument synthesis.',
