    description: 'Mid-2000s progressive-metal subgenre developed through Meshuggah-derived polymetric-rhythmic-and-down-tuned guitar production (the term "djent" is onomatopoeic for the distinctive percussive palm-muted heavily-distorted seven-or-eight-string guitar attack). Periphery (Misha Mansoor, founded 2005), Animals As Leaders (Tosin Abasi), TesseracT, Monuments, and the broader Sumerian Records and Basick Records label rosters anchor the canonical djent roster.',
