    description: 'The Chinese rice-planting song (chayang-diao, 插秧调 — also chayanggewu 插秧歌舞 in some regional traditions) tradition continuous from premodern Chinese-agricultural village-labor practice across rice-growing Southern China (Hunan, Jiangsu, Fujian, Jiangxi, Sichuan, Yunnan all have distinct regional chayang-diao traditions) through 20th-century Chinese-folklorist documentation (the 1950s-1960s Chinese-Communist-Party folk-collection-and-codification movement documented chayang-diao corpus as canonical "people\'s-art") into modern Chinese-rural-and-folk-revival practice. Defined by call-and-response group-vocal foreground with dizi-and-sheng optional-accompaniment, Mandarin-and-regional-Chinese-language text register, Chinese-pentatonic modal vocabulary, characteristic rice-paddy task-coordination structure.',
    exemplars: ['Hunan chayang-diao traditional rice-planting canonical', 'Jiangsu chayang-diao traditional canonical', 'Fujian regional rice-planting song traditional canonical', 'Yang Liping — modern Chinese-folk-dance with chayang-diao-derived rep', 'Chinese rural village rice-planting continuous-living tradition'],
