    description: 'The Indonesian rice-planting song tradition across Javanese, Sundanese, Balinese, Sumatran-Minangkabau, and Sulawesi regional-cultures continuous from premodern Indonesian-agricultural village-labor practice through colonial-period continuous performance into modern Indonesian-rural continuous practice; the Indonesian rice-paddy planting and harvest-songs integrate gamelan-and-vocal arrangements distinct to each regional culture, with Javanese rice-planting song notably integrating slendro-and-pelog tunings, Sundanese rice-songs using kacapi-and-suling accompaniment, Balinese rice-songs integrating with broader Balinese-temple-ritual context. Defined by slendro-pelog tuning vocabulary, regional-Indonesian language text register, characteristic call-and-response group-vocal arrangement, characteristic rice-paddy task-coordination structure.',
    exemplars: ['Javanese village rice-planting song traditional canonical', 'Balinese rice-planting song integrated with Subak irrigation-ritual', 'Sundanese rice-planting song traditional with kacapi-suling', 'Sumatran-Minangkabau rice-harvest song traditional', 'Sulawesi-Toraja rice-planting song traditional'],
